      "summary": "Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Embracing Digital Transformation The Evidence / Who &mdash; In-depth interviews and case studies with real-world leaders validating architecture patterns and sharing transformation lessons. Transformation Architecture Hub All Shows Overview The Canon (DTA) Weekly News (EDTW) All Episodes #394 How to Control AI With Data-First Governance 0 Tim Freestone argues that AI is not leveling the playing field; it is magnifying the gaps organizations already had in data management, cybersecurity control, and operational discipline. The real issue is not whether companies adopt AI, but whether they can govern it around specific business outcomes and data controls. Leaders who focus on broad mandates or vanity metrics will create noise, not value. The better path is controlled deployment, domain expertise, and measurable use cases tied to real business inputs and outputs. 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 Watch Now #393 How to Build AI Workflows Without Burning Out Your Team 0 This conversation is about more than workplace wellbeing. It is a warning to leaders that technology adoption changes the load on people, not just the output of systems. Georgina Woodley argues that AI can accelerate work while quietly increasing pressure, decision fatigue, and organizational friction. The leadership lesson is straightforward: if executives want AI to create durable value, they have to manage the human system with the same discipline they apply to the technical stack. 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 Watch Now Listen Now #392 How to Build AI ",
