      "summary": "Accountability as an architectural concern | Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Skip to content Home Episodes Episode 15: Accountability as an architectural concern Episode 15 Accountability as an architectural concern 2026-04-22 Hosted by Dr. Darren Pulsipher Explore more in the episode archive . Summary In the world of digital transformation, organizations often encounter challenges related to accountability. These challenges, if not addressed properly, can hinder the progress of transformation initiatives. In his lecture “Accountability as an Architectural Concern,” Dr. Darren discusses how accountability should be viewed not merely as a behavioral issue, but as a fundamental aspect of organizational architecture. Darren W Pulsipher In the world of digital transformation, organizations often encounter challenges related to accountability. These challenges, if not addressed properly, can hinder the progress of transformation initiatives. In his lecture “Accountability as an Architectural Concern,” Dr. Darren discusses how accountability should be viewed not merely as a behavioral issue, but as a fundamental aspect of organizational architecture. Copyright &copy; Paidar Productions LLC All rights reserved",
